  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Copying lists"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "list2 = list1 does not copy; both names refer to the same list, so a change through one is seen through the other. To make a real copy, use slicing list2 = list1[:], the list() function list2 = list(list1), or copy.copy(list1) from the copy module.",
    "kn": "list2 = list1 ನಕಲು ಮಾಡುವುದಿಲ್ಲ; ಎರಡೂ ಹೆಸರು ಒಂದೇ ಲಿಸ್ಟನ್ನು ಸೂಚಿಸುತ್ತವೆ. ನಿಜವಾದ ನಕಲಿಗೆ list1[:], list(list1) ಅಥವಾ copy.copy(list1) ಬಳಸಿ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Alias: same list, two names"
    },
    {
     "en": "Copy: new list with the same elements"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "list2 = list1 does not copy; both names refer to the same list, so a change through one is seen through the other. To make a real copy, use slicing list2 = list1[:], the list() function list2 = list(list1), or copy.copy(list1) from the copy module.",
    "kn": "list2 = list1 ನಕಲು ಮಾಡುವುದಿಲ್ಲ; ಎರಡೂ ಹೆಸರು ಒಂದೇ ಲಿಸ್ಟನ್ನು ಸೂಚಿಸುತ್ತವೆ. ನಿಜವಾದ ನಕಲಿಗೆ list1[:], list(list1) ಅಥವಾ copy.copy(list1) ಬಳಸಿ."
   }
